Unlucky, I suppose.  I've looked for Fort Ludios three times (the only
times I felt I had characters that were good enough) and found it three
times.  Up till now I thought it was there in _all_ games!

Spoilers...

To answer the original question, there is a secret door at the upper-left
corner of the room.  This leads to a treasure zoo.  After that, you enter
the main chamber, which contains a castle.  There is a huge barracks that
contains guards (soldiers, seargents, etc.) that try to prevent you from
getting to the castle, not to mention a few dragons swimming around the
moat.  The castle itself has a throne room full of... more monsters.
What makes things even harder is that all the monsters are awake when you
enter, even if you have stealth, thanks to their alarm system.  :(
Take advantage of the three bottlenecks in the fort; the soldiers will
be so busy hitting and zapping each other in their haste to attack you,
it'll be less trouble for you.

When/if you make it past everything, there are storerooms filled with
gold and gems.  Watch out for land mines, though.  What's good about this
level is that there are four guaranteed dragons swimming around outside.
Lure them out of the water and kill them.  Even if they don't leave scales
lying around, their corpses are good to eat (hint, hint).  Just make sure
you have some form of reflection when you take them on, or that black
dragon could spell trouble...
